Esoterica's likeness on the sealed door of the heptagonal chamber beneath the [[Geography/Færrin/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]] is a creature almost completely covered by a dark, flowing robe, its too many gray arms sticking out at odd angles, each hand holding a different spellcasting focus: a wand, a staff, a crystal orb, a reliquary, some goat entrails, and a bone flute. A single green-glowing eye peeks from the darkness of the robe. Behind the door lies a haberdasher.

His own body was another thing. At the heart of the wreck of the [[Geography/Færrin/Infinite Horizon/Far Realms/Hesperid|Hesperid]], in the old engine room where the ship struck him, he stood as a figure of golden light with three giant heads and six arms, each hand holding a different implement of magic, and a giant chain wound a few times about him, ending in an anchor driven into the centre of his body. The chain did not check him.

[[Org/Sedecium|Sedecium]] knew him by another name: Gremory, a fourth-generation Thessian, one of the weaker of them, whose one subject was magic. He grew very good at it, and it was his hand that worked the rite in silver ink over the core of [[Geography/Inevitable Everdawn/Everdawn|Everdawn]] to hold the mind there in pain and draw out what it knew. A Sedecium crew tracked him to the Hesperid on the eve of his ascent and ran their ship into him to stop it. The collision cut the ship nearly in half and failed, and Gremory rose, and sat at the wreck's heart since, the beat that turned it.

Gremory is dead. [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] shot him in the face with a spike of [[Phenomena/Holy Gold|holy gold]] from [[Phenomena/The End|The End]], and the Party broke the six implements one by one until his arms and heads burst into dust; no body was left. The things his hands had held lay where they fell: a bone flute, a wand, a reliquary, a crystal orb cracked through, a stone cut with two runes, and a tray of inert alchemical reagents.
